WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:01.849
Robert Baratheon: "Ours is the Fury."

00:00:01.849 --> 00:00:06.089
These are the words of the black stag of Baratheon.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:12.421
A battle cry echoed throughout the land in
rebellion, when I, Robert Baratheon, the First

00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:19.750
of His Name, seized the Iron Throne from the
Mad King, Aerys Targaryen, ending a dynasty

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.630
nearly three hundred years old.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:31.260
House Baratheon was born in the Wars of Conquest
when Aegon the Dragon invaded Westeros.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.180
Aegon sent his commander, Orys Baratheon,
to take Storm's End.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.850
Argilac the Arrogant, the last of the Storm
Kings, foolishly left the safety of his stronghold

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.370
and met the Baratheon warlord in open battle.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:53.870
Argilac was soundly defeated, and Orys took
his lands, his holdings, and his daughter.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:01:04.000
Orys was said to be a half-brother to Aegon
Targaryen.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:26.999
If this were true, a 
little blood of the dragon mingled with that

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:30.350
of the stag in those days.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:37.789
The seat of House Baratheon is Storm's End,
a legendary keep raised in the Age of Heroes.

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:43.130
It overlooks Shipbreaker Bay, where legend
has it that Durran, the first Storm King,

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:49.119
raised the keep with the aid of Bran the Builder
of House Stark, forging a centuries-long connection

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.229
with the Stormlands and the North.

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:56.719
After Aegon's conquest of the Seven Kingdoms,
the Baratheons remained loyal enough to the

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:00.420
crown while Targaryen kings came and went.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.959
But loyalty has its limits.

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:11.370
When Rhaegar Targaryen, Aerys' vile son and
heir, abducted Lyanna Stark, my betrothed,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.959
my beloved, it was time to act.

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:17.799
We raised our banners.

00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:24.069
Baratheon, Stark, Jon Arryn, and the Tullys,
united in rebellion against Rhaegar and his

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:26.959
father, the Mad King.

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:30.269
We were victorious and took the Iron Throne.

00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:36.670
That bit of dragon blood in my veins came
in well as it made me a distant relation to

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:42.310
the Targaryen dynasty blood of my long-lost
ancestor, Orys.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.870
The truth of it is I took it.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.629
Brienne of Tarth: Tarth has lulled many a
novice sailor into complacency.

00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:54.329
Our lush island sits on calm blue water like
an emerald set into a sapphire.

00:02:54.329 --> 00:02:58.780
You would never guess that such a vision is
only the sheath hiding the blade of Shipbreaker

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:04.519
Bay, with its treacherous tides, unpredictable
gales, and sharp rocks lurking just below

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:06.540
the water's surface.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.980
The storms that blow through the bay water
the Kingswood and Rainwood, two of the great

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:16.269
forests of Westeros, and they give the Stormlands
their name.

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:20.959
Even without our weather, we have more than
earned our name in strife.

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:27.530
The first Storm King, Durran, started his
reign by declaring war on the gods themselves.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.730
He loved the daughter of the sea god and the
wind goddess, but they forbade the union.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:36.900
At their wedding, the gods unleashed their
might, pulling down his hold and killing all

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:41.630
of Durran's family and guests, though his
wife shielded him.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:47.909
Durran vowed to rebuild, and when he did,
the gods again destroyed his home.

00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:53.140
His councilors begged him to retreat inland,
but he would not abandon his war.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.219
Finally, with the council of the Children
of the Forest, or perhaps a young Bran the

00:03:57.219 --> 00:04:03.670
Builder, Durran raised a seventh castle that,
try as they might and still do, the wind and

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.019
sea gods could not tear asunder.

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:12.719
Durran took the name Godsgrief and called
his new home Storm's End.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:17.670
Having beaten the waters to the east, the
Storm Kings turned their gaze to more practical

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:21.870
enemies, the Reach, the Riverlands, and Dorne.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.890
For thousands of years, the Storm Kings fought
the Gardener Kings of the Reach and various

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:31.860
families of Dorne for control of the Dornish
Marches, just below the Red Mountains.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:36.750
The fighting did not stop until Dorne married
into the Seven Kingdoms, a mere hundred years

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.750
ago.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:42.910
But still, the houses of the Stormlands, such
as the Dondarrions, guard the Boneway, the

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:47.620
mountain pass into the Marches, against any
Dornish incursion.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.360
The Storm Kings had greater luck to their
north at first.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.290
They took the Trident from the River Kings
and built an empire that stretched as far

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:57.290
as the Neck.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:02.380
But then the ironborn swarmed out of their
islands and pushed the Storm Kings out of

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.380
the Riverlands.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:09.090
No doubt, the ironborn intended to expand
their empire into the Stormlands.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:13.730
Before they had a chance, Aegon Targaryen
landed with his dragons.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:20.390
While Aegon burned the kings of the Iron Islands,
the Rock and the Reach, his fiercest commander

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:26.170
and rumored bastard brother, Orys Baratheon,
set out to subdue the Stormlands.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:31.330
No matter how fierce a warrior he was, no
one could have envied his task.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:36.751
Storm's End had seen thousands of years of
war and never fallen, but Argilac, the Storm

00:05:36.751 --> 00:05:41.750
King, chose not to barricade himself behind
its walls and gave Orys the battle he must

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.630
have hoped for.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:52.470
Orys slew Argilac and took Argilac's castle,
kingdom, daughter, sigil, and House words.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:56.100
House Baratheon became the Lord of the Stormlands.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:01.290
Targaryen rule quieted the Stormlands for
the most part until Robert rebelled against

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.400
the Mad King.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.840
His first challenge came not from the Crown,
but from his own bannermen who tried to join

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.110
forces against him.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:15.290
Robert struck first, defeating three armies
in a single day at Summerhall.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:19.530
The victory cemented Robert's control of the
Stormlands, and he was able to march on the

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:23.470
Reach and Riverlands with no enemy to his
rear.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:27.210
Yet not all of Robert's bannermen sided with
him.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:33.330
Ser Barristan the Bold came from the Stormlands,
but as the preeminent member of Aerys's kingsguard

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.770
and greatest knight in the realm, Ser Barristan
remained loyal.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.340
After Robert's decisive victory on the Trident,
Robert sent his own maester to care for his

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.750
countryman Ser Barristan, who had suffered
grievous wounds while fighting so hard to

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.300
kill him.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:54.750
Later, when the Kingslayer betrayed Aerys,
Robert pardoned Ser Barristan and even took

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.100
him onto his own kingsguard.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:03.670
When Robert lifted Mace Tyrell's ill-managed
Siege of Storm's End and returned to his ancestral

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:10.220
home, he realized the dream of all the Stormlords
before him – to rule the Seven Kingdoms.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.130
Robert Baratheon: Rebellion!

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:19.960
The crimes of House Targaryen were too heinous
to go unanswered.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:26.250
The noble Houses of Baratheon, Stark, and
Arryn, united to oppose and overthrow the

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.000
line of the cursed dragon kings.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.390
While Ned Stark and Arryn secured an alliance
with the Tullys of Riverrun, I called the

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:42.690
banners of Storm's End and rode out in force
against the Mad King and his minions.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.780
Gods, those were some battles!

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:52.180
Our first victory occurred at Summerhall where
I faced off against an army of dragon loyalists

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:56.630
and won three battles in a single day, three
in one day!

00:07:56.630 --> 00:08:00.920
Seven hells, that was a glorious day!

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:06.520
We tried to take Ashford Castle in the Reach,
but the Tyrells beat us back.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.530
We had to regroup.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:15.200
My army was pursued north by Aerys's army
and took refuge in the Stoney Sept in the

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.200
Riverlands.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:21.820
When the Targaryen army entered the town,
the sept bells tolled, a signal to the townspeople

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.710
of the battle that was to come.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:30.630
As the Targaryens searched from house to house
for me, the combined forces of Ned Stark and

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.920
the Tullys swept into the city.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:36.760
Gods, what a day that was!

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:40.830
It's now known as the Battle of the Bells.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:48.470
We overwhelmed the Mad King's forces and sent
them scampering back to King's Landing.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:54.070
Aerys's son, Rhaegar, who started the whole
damn thing, finally emerged from hiding in

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:57.141
the South and assembled his own army to face
us.

00:08:57.141 --> 00:09:03.540
As for the Mad King, he must have been pissing
himself.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:08.040
The battle that would decide the fate of the
Seven Kingdoms occurred at the crossing of

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.250
the Green Fork of the Trident river.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:17.070
Rhaegar commanded the royal host, which was
some forty thousand strong.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:23.920
My forces were outnumbered by nearly five
thousand men, but that didn't matter.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:31.110
They were fresh, but we were battle-hardened
and had justice on our side.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:34.820
As the battle raged around us, I faced off
with Rhaegar.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:40.310
The stag and the dragon right there in the
ford of the river.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:46.730
I fought with the fury of ten men, raining
blow after blow upon that vile prince before

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.670
burying my war hammer in his chest.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:55.170
I hit him so hard, the rubies on his armor
broke free, flinging them into the stream.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.950
They call it the Ruby Ford now.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:04.870
With that scum Rhaegar dead and the royal
army shattered, our next move was to make

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.340
for King's Landing.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.460
But I'd sustained a few wounds in the battle
and was unable to ride.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:21.690
I sent Ned Stark to the capital to face the
Mad King and make him pay 

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:33.820
for his crimes.

